        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_Head%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town's name comes from its position at the head of Barnegat Bay and early Bayhead Land Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_Head%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A railroad sign in the 1880s labeled the station \"Bay Head,\" and the name stuck when the borough was incorporated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_Head%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bay Head Historic District, listed in 2005, contains over 550 structures, making it one of New Jersey's largest historic districts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_Head%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "NJ Transit trains terminate at Bay Head station and yard, offering service north to Penn Station New York.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
